Version 4.1
SHEET 1 880 680
WIRE 208 160 192 160
FLAG 208 160 SineWave
FLAG 288 160 0
SYMBOL breakpoint 176 160 R0
SYMATTR Value start=300ms step=0.1n count=0
SYMATTR Value2 stop={start+50n}
SYMATTR Description Breakpoints to force smaller timesteps at specific times
SYMATTR InstName U1
TEXT 128 200 Left 2 !.tran 0 400m 0 0.1m
TEXT 152 80 Left 2 ;The sense of the breakpoint device is to \nmake simulation  timepoints more dense at\na specific range to increase accuracy\n(e.g for measuring narrow energyspikes)
TEXT 240 136 Left 2 !B0 dummy 0 v={time} tripdv=1 tripdt=1
TEXT 248 176 Left 2 ;count=500 -> step*count = 50ns sum\ncount=0 stop=start+50n = 50ns sum
